{title: In Peace I Lie Down}
{subtitle: Psalms 4:9}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm] [Gm/Bb] | [Ab] [Bb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Close your [Bb/D]eyes, the day is [Cm]done
The [Gm/Bb]stars are [Ab]out, the [Bb]night has [Eb]come
In [Ab]peace I [Bb]will lie down and [Eb]sleep
For you a[Bb]lone, Lord, make me [Eb]safe
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sleep, my little [Bb]one, sleep
[Cm]He who keeps you will not [Gm]slumber
[Ab]Sleep, my little [Eb]one, [Bb/D][Cm]sleep
[Fm7]He will [Bb]never [Eb]sleep
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The moon is [Bb/D]watching from the [Cm]sky
The [Ebmaj7/Bb]wind is [Ab]singing [Bb]lulla[Eb]by
In [Ab]peace I [Bb]will lie down and [Eb]sleep
For you a[Bb]lone, Lord, make me [Eb]safe
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sleep, my little [Bb]one, sleep
[Cm]He who keeps you will not [Gm]slumber
[Ab]Sleep, my little [Eb]one, [Bb/D][Cm]sleep
[Fm]He will [Bb]never [Eb]sleep
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Outro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Cm] |
| [Gm] | [Ab] | [Eb] [Bb/D] [Cm] | [Fm] [Bb] |
| [Eb] | [Eb] |
